title: Managing an Academic Software Project
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Sam
    family-names: Mangham
  - given-names: Steve
    family-names: Crouch
abstract: >-
    This course is designed to introduce academics to project management in a light and flexible way, providing basic guidance on breaking a project into tasks to be prioritised and tracked.
    It also covers software sustainability, encouraging best practise like clear coding and issue management, as well as the use of DOIs and releases to enable easy citation.
